@title Terminal rows: Draw no longer lists them, the terminal right-click menu does
@area Terminals
@sizes 1366x768
# Lane V4j (docs/design/visual-redesign.md section 6). The seven Draw > Terminals rows (Connect and
# Disconnect terminals, Toggle PE terminal, Reset PE override, strip number Up, Down and Lowest free)
# act on the terminals selected on the page. Their home is the right-click menu of a selected terminal,
# which already carried every one; Ctrl+K still runs them.
# The terminal-strips lesson supplies the drawn terminals: walk it to the step that selects two.
key ctrl+k
wait 4
text terminal strips
wait 6
key Enter
wait 40
shot 01-lesson-start
try click_text "Next"
wait 20
try click_text "Do it for me"
wait 30
try click_text "Do it for me"
wait 30
try click_text "Do it for me"
wait 30
try click_text "Do it for me"
wait 30
try click_text "Next"
wait 20
try click_text "Do it for me"
wait 30
expect "2 selected"
click 553 414 right
wait 10
shot 02-terminal-right-click-menu
expect "Connect terminals"
expect "Disconnect terminals"
expect "Strip number"
check_layout
key Escape
wait 4
click_text Draw #1
wait 6
shot 03-draw-menu
expect_not "Disconnect terminals"
expect_not "Toggle PE terminal"
expect_not "Reset PE override"
key Escape
wait 4
key ctrl+k
wait 6
text "disconnect terminals"
wait 8
shot 04-palette-path
expect "Terminal right-click menu"
key Escape
wait 4
